# Prizo Privacy Policy

**Last updated:** November 9, 2026

Persian version (for most users): [PRIVACY.md](PRIVACY.md)

This policy covers two products by the same developer:

* **Prizo browser extension** (Chrome Web Store): helps shoppers compare and monitor prices on Digikala and other supported Iranian stores.
* **Prizo for Android** (package `ir.prizo.android`): a browser for Digikala with the same kind of price tools.

Prizo is independent. It does not belong to Digikala or to any other store it works with.

## 1. The short version

* Prizo has no account system and no server of its own that receives your data. We found no code in either product that sends your data to a Prizo-operated server.
* Neither product contains analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting tools.
* Your watchlists, price history, settings, and similar data are stored on your own device or browser.
* To work, Prizo contacts the stores and services listed in section 4, and some of what you do reaches them (for example, a product ID or a search phrase).
* Prizo may earn a commission through affiliate links when you shop. This is described in section 5. It cannot be switched off in either product.

## 2. What Prizo stores on your device

### 2.1 Browser extension

Stored with `chrome.storage.local`, IndexedDB, and `localStorage`. Nothing is stored with `chrome.storage.sync`, so Prizo does not use Google's sync for it.

* **Watchlists and monitoring:** products, watched pages, watched flash sales and supermarket monitors with their conditions (target price, minimum discount, and so on), the latest results, and your notification messages. A supermarket monitor includes the place you chose (name and coordinates) and the stores you selected.
* **Price history:** prices Prizo observed for products, store snapshots, and deal observations.
* **Order analytics (only if you use it):** Digikala order records and order details that you load into the "order analysis" page, stored in IndexedDB as Digikala returns them, together with the Digikala account identifier and label they belong to. This data is not included in Prizo's backup file.
* **Preferences and tools:** feature toggles, theme, notification settings, work-hours settings (your monthly income and monthly work hours, if you enter them), Smart Cart shipping overrides and observations, and a journal of your last Smart Cart changes.

### 2.2 Android app

* **Local database:** watched pages and their products, and Flash Sale Watch conditions, results, and items.
* **App settings:** feature toggles, your watched products with their alert settings and recent prices, work-hours settings (your monthly income and hours, if you enter them), the last Smart Cart result and a journal of your last Smart Cart changes (product names, sellers, prices, quantities), and other app preferences.
* **Browser profile:** the app opens Digikala in a built-in browser, which keeps cookies, including your Digikala login, and the usual site storage and cache on the device. Product images are cached.

### 2.3 Backups

* **Android:** the app allows Android's automatic backup. The local database and the app settings can therefore be copied to your Google account backup and to a new device. Your login (the built-in browser profile) is excluded from backup and device transfer. You can turn backup off in Android settings.
* **Extension:** you can export a backup file from the settings page. The file is plain, unencrypted JSON, so keep it private.

## 3. Your Digikala and other store accounts

* You sign in on the store's own page. Prizo does not collect or store your Digikala password.
* **Extension:** to call Digikala's account features, the extension reads the Digikala `ACCESS_TOKEN` cookie through the `cookies` permission, and decodes it to identify the account (used to label stored orders). It does not store the token itself. For the supermarket address picker it also reads Okala's token cookie, and, only after you click and grant the optional permission, the sign-in data of an open Snapp Market tab. These are sent only to the same service they belong to, and saved addresses are used to fill the place picker and are not stored. Only the place you choose for a watch is stored.
* **Android:** features that need your account (vouchers, Smart Cart) use your Digikala login from the built-in browser and send it only to Digikala's API.
* **Smart Cart** can change your real Digikala cart (add, change, or remove items), but only after you confirm a list of changes.
* Background checks (watchlist, watched pages, flash sales) in the Android app use public requests without your login.

## 4. Who Prizo contacts, and what they receive

Whenever a request is made, the receiving server also sees your IP address and ordinary request details.

* **Digikala** (api.digikala.com, www.digikala.com): product IDs, page addresses of what you watch, and, for account features, your own session. The extension also reads Digikala product pages directly in some cases.
* **Other supported stores** (extension: Snapp Shop, Janebi, Technolife, Khanoumi, Lion Computer, Basalam, Banimode, Digistyle, Modiseh, Zanbil, Snapp Market): product IDs and search addresses, for the products and pages you watch or open.
* **Supermarket services** (extension: Okala, Snapp Market, Digikala Hypermarket through api.digikalajet.ir): the coordinates of the place you chose, store IDs, and search text.
* **Torob** (api.torob.com): the product title (which you can edit in the Android app) when you use the Torob comparison. Results open on torob.com.
* **Affiliate networks:** see section 5.
* **GitHub** (extension): when you open the Gadget Store tab, the extension downloads a configuration file from raw.githubusercontent.com. GitHub sees your IP address. The file can contain a third-party widget script from Affilio, which runs in an isolated sandboxed page.
* **Google** (extension): at startup the extension makes a connection test to www.google.com. No user data is sent, but Google sees the IP address.
* **Payment and group sites (Android):** the built-in browser opens Digikala, its group sites (Digikala Jet, Digistyle), and payment pages (Digipay, bank gateways) inside the app. These are their own websites with their own policies. Other links open in your system browser.

Prizo does not send your watchlists, price history, income, work hours, or order data to anyone except as part of the requests described above.

## 5. Affiliate links and support for Prizo

Prizo is free. It is supported through affiliate links: when you buy after arriving through such a link, the store or network may pay Prizo a commission. It does not change the price you pay.

* **Extension:** Prizo rewrites Digikala product links on pages into affiliate links (through aflo.ir, run by Affilio), and uses affiliate links for cart actions and comparison links on several stores (aflo.ir and deemanetwork.com). Digikala Fresh and Supermarket are excluded. The settings page tells you this is always on; there is no switch.
* **Android:** when Prizo opens Digikala at the app's entry points (for example a link you share to Prizo, or its start page), it goes through an aflo.ir link. Digikala Fresh and the supermarket section are excluded. There is no switch. The affiliate sites load inside the app, and their cookies live in the built-in browser profile.
* The affiliate network sees the address you were going to open (such as a product, search, or cart link). Prizo does not add your watchlists or any other personal data to it.

## 6. Permissions

### 6.1 Extension

* **storage, unlimitedStorage:** keep your data on the device, including large price histories.
* **notifications:** alert you to price changes.
* **alarms:** run scheduled checks.
* **tabs, activeTab, scripting:** work with supported store pages; the extension also reads the address of open tabs to show its icon and badge and to guard affiliate navigation, but it acts only on supported sites and does not store tab addresses. `scripting` is also used to read Snapp Market sign-in data after you click.
* **cookies:** read (never write) Digikala and Okala session cookies, as described in section 3.
* **Host permissions:** the stores and services in section 4. Snapp Market access is optional.

### 6.2 Android

* **INTERNET:** load pages and make the requests above.
* **ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE:** tell "no connection" apart from a site error.
* **POST_NOTIFICATIONS:** show alerts.
* **RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED:** let scheduled checks continue after a restart.
* The app asks for no location, contacts, camera, microphone, or storage access.
* The app can receive a Digikala link you share to it. It reads only a digikala.com link from the shared text and does not store the text.

## 7. Your choices and deleting data

* **Extension:** remove products, pages, and monitors one by one; clear price history, store data, deal observations, and order analytics from Storage Management; turn features off in settings; export or import a backup. There is no single "delete everything" button; removing the extension from the browser deletes its data.
* **Android:** remove watched products, pages, and flash alerts in the app (a flash alert's results are deleted with it); turn features off in settings. There is no in-app "clear all" or sign-out button. To delete everything, use Android's "Clear storage" for Prizo or uninstall it.
* Because Prizo holds no account or server copy of your data, there is nothing for us to delete on our side. Data held by Digikala, Torob, and other services is subject to their own policies.

## 8. Children

Prizo is not aimed at children and does not knowingly collect their personal information.

## 9. Security

Your data stays on your device, which reduces what can leak, but no software is perfectly secure. Keep your browser, phone, and backup files protected and up to date.

## 10. Changes

When Prizo's data handling changes, this policy will be updated in this repository, with a new date at the top.

